# CLAMP core

- Product: delegation control for AI agents that spend. Outcomes: Allow, Block, Needs human.
- Organiser hero: Kiln parse or explain (Song) plus Base Sepolia on chain receipts (Henry).
- Henry owns frontend, sessions, metrics UI, on chain mandate or decision receipts, README.
- Song owns Kiln client, gate, metering, AuditTrail shape. Do not implement Song work in Henry passes.
- Fail closed if Song APIs are unwired. No fake Kiln, no mock pays, no invented tx hashes.
- No localStorage or sessionStorage for product state. Use signed server sessions and tenant scoping.
- Never claim unhackable. Prefer hard controls and an inspectable trail.
- AgentRouter, Tavily, and TinyFish are not on the spend path.
